# AHS — layered muguet add-only card

**F240/N60 — 2026-09-07 — BENCH-TRIAL PROPOSAL**  
Not a validated rescue, skin-use or release approval.

For the confirmed parent with DHM 200 µL neat and Helional 100 µL neat; all other v3 amounts unchanged. No Mayol addition was reported. This is an alternative to that earlier proposal, not a correction to stack on top of it.

## Add only these — Basket 7, descending raw volume

| Order | Material | Stock | Separate 5.00 mL trial | Untouched 30.00 mL equivalent |
|---:|---|---|---:|---:|
| 1 | Florol | Neat/as supplied | 40 µL (0.040 mL) | 240 µL (0.240 mL) |
| 2 | Nympheal | Neat/as supplied | 10 µL (0.010 mL) | 60 µL (0.060 mL) |
| | **Total addition** | | **50 µL** | **300 µL** |
| | **Nominal resulting volume** | | **5.050 mL** | **30.300 mL** |

These columns are alternative scales, not successive additions. All other baskets are skipped. No extra Helional, DHM, Hedione, Mayol, Calone, musk, wood, salicylate, ethanol or carrier.

Florol is the proposed soft petal-body addition; the smaller Nympheal addition tests watery-floral definition/density. Existing Helional/Hedione/salicylate/wood/musk structure supplies the other layers. The 4:1 stock-volume ratio is exploratory, not a proven optimum or smell-strength ratio.

## Preserve the bottle

Use a separate 5 mL trial rather than automatically changing the full bottle. Accurate 10 µL dispensing is required; do not use drops or round up. Label the sample; compare with untreated perfume on blotters using equal applications/preparation age at opening, 5 min, 30 min, then 2 h/4 h. Reject soapiness, detached floral density, obscured mandarin or no useful improvement. No skin/spray-use clearance is asserted.

If exactly 5 mL was removed from exactly 30 mL and nothing else was withdrawn/sprayed, the 25 mL remainder would scale to 200 µL Florol + 50 µL Nympheal, nominal 25.250 mL. Other withdrawals require rescaling. Do not automatically return the sample or give a second dose to treated material.

## Evidence

Fresh parent-linked G15 dose-continuity screen: **PASS**, with parent and temporal comparisons present. Overall diagnostic: **FAIL — 103 PASS / 35 WARN / 9 FAIL / 1 SKIP**. See [complete resulting formula and analysis](AHS_UserBottle_MuguetLayered_F240_N60_20260907.md), [canonical record](records/AHS_UserBottle_MuguetLayered_20260907.json) and [verification receipt](../docs/verification/AHS_MuguetLayered_20260907_review.json). The full formula lists existing contents for checking, not ingredients to add again.

Nympheal is marked HAVE in the source register, but its “as supplied; product basis” wording is unresolved by the stock gate. This is not evidence of physical absence. The proposed supplied-stock transfer is conditional on that stock identity/form; quantitative and release authority remain HOLD. Do not promote this card to a validated compounding or whole-bottle release instruction.

Both new-material ODTs are unverified; physical-property conflicts remain. Raw stock volumes do not supply exact active masses/ppm w/w. The model cannot prove punch, balance or safety. Safety/release remain HOLD, sensory effect NOT TESTED.

Use suitable gloves/eye protection and ventilation, avoid concentrated contact/mist, and keep alcohol away from ignition.
